mxNZEhEaTh4MHU3NEhEVmFzMTkwNkczRkJYblV2dWZPOWtfbjdXNUl2d2R0d0prMDNEb1o0UzFRemhhWnhxeEdqejFsRmNB?oc=5","date":"2026-10-20","zh":"Cloudflare 的 Clairic 比 LLM 更快、更便宜地從文件中提取數據"},{"title":"Cloudflare (NYSE:NET) Stock Forecast & Analyst Predictions","src":"Simply Wall Street","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMidkFVX3lxTFBqM2t5UjBGOTdMbHloN1JqYVJCZFVZZlVyblNWMUFjUTlUUkRsSVpaVi1XQXl0eldrc2wwTGp3MHA1YVQ0SjhSR1EtRDFGRDhva0REVE9DYmVWX0EzbExtREtUZkwzRDZuQjJ5eFhPNnFrWFBDTHc?oc=5","date":"2026-10-20","zh":"Cloudflare (NYSE:NET) 股票預測與分析師預測"}],"themes":[{"name":"雲端/軟體","count":13},{"name":"AI 人工智慧","count":3},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":3},{"name":"財報","count":2},{"name":"分析師評等","count":2},{"name":"減重藥/生技","count":1},{"name":"股票回購/股利","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-26","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1477333/000147733326000016/cloud-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Over the past decade, the technology industry has been undergoing a massive transition from on-premises hardware and software that customers buy, to services in the cloud that they rent. Organizations find themselves at different points in this transition to the cloud. Regardless of where organizations are in their transition, they all face a common set of challenges: they exist in a complex, heterogeneous infrastructure environment which exacerbates the fundamental problems of the Internet more than ever, and the on-premises hardware boxes that they once relied upon to solve these problems were never designed to work in such an environment. As more workloads move to the cloud and workforces become increasingly distributed globally, there is no point in installing additional hardware boxes on premise. An on-premises box will not solve the problems organizations now face. Nor can a busine","zh":"在過去的十年中，科技業經歷了從客戶購買的本地硬體和軟體到他們租用的雲端服務的巨大轉變。組織發現自己在向雲端過渡的過程中處於不同的階段。無論組織處於轉型的哪個階段，它們都面臨著一系列共同的挑戰：它們存在於複雜的異質基礎設施環境中，這比以往任何時候都更加加劇了互聯網的基本問題，而它們曾經依賴於解決這些問題的本地硬體盒從來沒有被設計用於在這樣的環境中工作。隨著越來越多的工作負載轉移到雲端，並且勞動力越來越分佈在全球範圍內，在本地安裝額外的硬體盒已經沒有意義了。本地盒子無法解決組織現在面臨的問題。企業也不可以"},{"en":"The result is that a major architectural shift at the network layer is underway. Previously, enterprises would often string together a diverse set of on-premises hardware boxes from different vendors to solve their network challenges. As these solutions move to the cloud, the network latency, support complexity, and cost of overhead makes stringing together multiple point-cloud solutions that only address specific network needs also untenable. Customers are therefore looking to consolidate behind a single, global provider that operates in the cloud — what has been described as a \"Connectivity Cloud\".","zh":"结果是网络层的重大架构转变正在进行。以前，企业通常会将来自不同供应商的各种本地硬件盒组合在一起来解决网络挑战。隨著這些解決方案遷移到雲端，網路延遲、支援複雜性和管理成本使得將多個僅滿足特定網路需求的點雲解決方案串在一起也是站不住腳的。因此，客户希望整合在云中运营的单一全球提供商——即所谓的“连接云”。"},{"en":"Cloudflare is a leader in this Connectivity Cloud category. We deliver a broad range of services to businesses of all sizes and in all geographies — making them more secure, enhancing the performance of their business-critical applications, and eliminating the cost and complexity of managing individual network hardware. Our network serves as a scalable, easy-to-use, unified control plane to deliver security, performance, and reliability across on-premises, hybrid, cloud, and software-as-a-service (SaaS) applications. We serve comprehensive customer needs across security and connectivity, and increasingly, the distributed and programmable nature of our network is resulting in customers building their applications on top of our network, too — including both traditional applications and those that are enhanced with artificial intelligence (AI).","zh":"Cloudflare 是該連結雲端類別的領導者。我們為各種規模、各個地區的企業提供廣泛的服務，使它們更加安全，提高關鍵業務應用程式的效能，並消除管理單一網路硬體的成本和複雜性。我們的網路作為一個可擴展、易於使用的統一控制平面，可為本地、混合、雲端和軟體即服務 (SaaS) 應用程式提供安全性、效能和可靠性。我們滿足安全和連接方面的全面客戶需求，而且我們網路的分散式和可編程特性也越來越多地導致客戶在我們的網路之上構建他們的應用程式 - 包括傳統應用程式和透過人工智慧 (AI) 增強的應用程式。"}],"markets":[{"en":"We deliver a suite of deeply integrated products that serve as a unified control plane for our customers, allowing them to build, connect, and secure applications and corporate infrastructure. Customers can quickly and easily join Cloudflare by using just one of our products and then expand their usage of Cloudflare over time by adding additional products. Our full suite of products consists of (1) our application services that help deliver security, performance, and reliability for any organization's applications connected to the Internet, including websites and application programming interfaces (APIs), and that also form the foundation of our newly announced efforts to allow content creators to monetize their work by controlling how bots, crawlers, and agents access their work; (2) our secure access service edge (SASE) platform, which contains our suite of Zero Trust and workplace sec","zh":"我們提供一套深度整合的產品，作為客戶的統一控制平面，使他們能夠建置、連接和保護應用程式和企業基礎設施。客戶只需使用我們的產品即可快速輕鬆地加入 Cloudflare，然後隨著時間的推移透過添加其他產品來擴大 Cloudflare 的使用範圍。我們的全套產品包括 (1) 我們的應用程式服務，幫助為連接到互聯網的任何組織的應用程式提供安全性、性能和可靠性，包括網站和應用程式介面 (API)，並且這也構成了我們新宣布的努力的基礎，即允許內容創建者透過控制機器人、爬蟲和代理存取其工作的方式來貨幣化他們的工作；"},{"en":"build and deploy serverless and AI applications with scale, performance, security and reliability: and (4) our consumer offerings.","zh":""}],"customers":[{"en":"We view our millions of free and paying customers, which manage millions of Internet properties on our network, as part of a broad, global community.","zh":"我們將數以百萬計的免費和付費客戶視為廣泛的全球社群的一部分，他們管理著我們網路上的數百萬個網路資產。"},{"en":"As of December 31, 2025, we had approximately 332,000 paying customers across more than 190 countries. Our paying customer base is highly diversified across organizations of all sizes in every major industry vertical including technology, healthcare, financial services, consumer and retail, industrial, non-profit, and government. Our large customer count has increased from 2,756 as of December 31, 2023 to 3,497 as of December 31, 2024 to 4,298 as of December 31, 2025. Refer to Part II, Item 7, Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations for additional information regarding the definitions of our \"paying customers\" and \"large customers.\"","zh":"截至 2025 年 12 月 31 日，我们在 190 多个国家/地区拥有约 332,000 名付费客户。我們的付費客戶群高度多元化，涵蓋各個主要垂直行業的各種規模的組織，包括技術、醫療保健、金融服務、消費者和零售、工業、非營利組織和政府。我們的大客戶數量已從截至2023年12月31日的2,756家增加到截至2024年12月31日的3,497家，再增加到截至2025年12月31日的4,298家。有關我們的「付費客戶」和「大客戶」定義的更多資訊，請參閱第二部分第7項，管理層對財務狀況和經營業績的討論和分析。"}],"competition":[{"en":"On-premises network hardware vendors. We compete with companies in this category to provide security, performance, and reliability services. We believe we are positioned favorably against these vendors with our cloud-based, multitenant approach that is better suited to an increasingly cloud-based world and that allows customers to treat our services as operational as opposed to capital costs.","zh":"本地網路硬體供應商。我們與此類公司競爭，提供安全、效能和可靠性服務。我們相信，憑藉基於雲端的多租戶方法，我們在與這些供應商的競爭中處於有利地位，這種方法更適合日益基於雲端的世界，並且允許客戶將我們的服務視為可操作的服務，而不是資本成本。"},{"en":"Point solution vendors, which provide cloud-based products and services to address a single use case or challenge, in various categories including application and network security vendors, content delivery network (CDN) vendors, domain name system (DNS) services vendors, email security vendors, and SD-WAN vendors. Providers in these categories are all focused on delivering cloud-based point solutions. However, customers are increasingly looking for an integrated infrastructure platform offering security, performance, and reliability through a single vendor.","zh":"單點解決方案供應商，提供基於雲端的產品和服務來解決單一用例或挑戰，包括應用程式和網路安全供應商、內容交付網路 (CDN) 供應商、網域名稱系統 (DNS) 服務供應商、電子郵件安全供應商和 SD-WAN 供應商。這些類別的提供者都專注於提供基於雲端的單點解決方案。然而，客戶越來越多地尋求透過單一供應商提供安全性、效能和可靠性的整合基礎設施平台。"}],"segments":{"geo":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"US","val":1072996000,"zh":"美國"},{"name":"EMEA","val":598624000,"zh":"歐洲、中東和非洲地區"},{"name":"Asia Pacific","val":329760000,"zh":"亞太"},{"name":"Other Geographical Regions","val":166557000,"zh":"其他地理區域"}],"total":2167937000}},"peers":["DDOG","CRWD","ZS","SNOW","OKTA"]}}